{"content":[{"c":["JUDAH (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Fourth of Jacob’s 12 sons (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.23","r":"Gen.35.23","rawR":"Gen.35.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.23","value":"Gen.35.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.1","r":"1Chr.2.1","rawR":"1Chr.2.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.1","value":"1Chr.2.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:1"},") and the fourth son born to Jacob by Leah, who, overjoyed with the thought of bearing Jacob another son, named him Judah, meaning “praise” (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.29.35","r":"Gen.29.35","rawR":"Gen.29.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.29.35","value":"Gen.29.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 29:35"},"). Judah fathered five sons: Er, Onan, and Shelah by Bathshua the Canaanitess (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.3-5","r":"Gen.38.3-5","rawR":"Gen.38.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.3-5","value":"Gen.38.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:3-5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.3","r":"1Chr.2.3","rawR":"1Chr.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.3","value":"1Chr.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:3"},"); and the twins Perez and Zerah by Tamar, his daughter-in-law (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.29-30","r":"Gen.38.29-30","rawR":"Gen.38.29-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.29-30","value":"Gen.38.29-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:29-30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.4","r":"1Chr.2.4","rawR":"1Chr.2.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.4","value":"1Chr.2.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:4"},"). He eventually settled his family in Egypt with his father and brothers (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.1.2","r":"Exod.1.2","rawR":"Exod.1.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.1.2","value":"Exod.1.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 1:2"},"), although his first two sons, Er and Onan, were divinely killed in Canaan for their disobedience (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.12","r":"Gen.46.12","rawR":"Gen.46.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.12","value":"Gen.46.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:12"},"). Judah became the founder of one of Israel’s 12 tribes (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.26-27","r":"Num.1.26-27","rawR":"Num.1.26-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.26-27","value":"Num.1.26-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:26-27"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["Though reckless in his behavior with Tamar (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.6-30","r":"Gen.38.6-30","rawR":"Gen.38.6-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.6-30","value":"Gen.38.6-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:6-30"},"), Judah showed firm resolve in taking personal responsibility for Benjamin’s safety in Egypt and acting as intercessor for his brothers before Joseph (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.44.14-18","r":"Gen.44.14-18","rawR":"Gen.44.14-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.44.14-18","value":"Gen.44.14-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:14-18"},"). At the time of Jacob’s blessing, Judah was granted the birthright privileges of the firstborn; the leadership of Jacob’s family would come through Judah’s seed, as would the promised Messiah of Abraham’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.49.8-12","r":"Gen.49.8-12","rawR":"Gen.49.8-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.49.8-12","value":"Gen.49.8-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"49:8-12"},"). Later, Judah’s family was praised at the time of Ruth’s engagement to Boaz (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.12","r":"Ruth.4.12","rawR":"Ruth.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.12","value":"Ruth.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 4:12"},"), and both the Davidic lines of kings (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.1-15","r":"1Chr.2.1-15","rawR":"1Chr.2.1-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.1-15","value":"1Chr.2.1-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:1-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.1-24","r":"1Chr.3.1-24","rawR":"1Chr.3.1-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.1-24","value":"1Chr.3.1-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:1-24"},") and Jesus Christ’s ancestors traced their descent from Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.2-3","r":"Matt.1.2-3","rawR":"Matt.1.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.2-3","value":"Matt.1.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:2-3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.33","r":"Luke.3.33","rawR":"Luke.3.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.33","value":"Luke.3.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"; ",{"href":"?item=JudahTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JudahTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JudahTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judah, Tribe of"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Forefather of a family of Levites who assisted Jeshua, the high priest, with rebuilding the temple during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.3.9","r":"Ezra.3.9","rawR":"Ezra.3.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.3.9","value":"Ezra.3.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 3:9"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). He is alternately called Hodaviah in ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.40","r":"Ezra.2.40","rawR":"Ezra.2.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.40","value":"Ezra.2.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 2:40"}," and Hodevah in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.43","r":"Neh.7.43","rawR":"Neh.7.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.43","value":"Neh.7.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 7:43"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Hodaviah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Hodaviah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Hodaviah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Hodaviah #4"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One of the Levites who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.23","r":"Ezra.10.23","rawR":"Ezra.10.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.23","value":"Ezra.10.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Benjamite, son of Hassenuah, who was second in command over the city of Jerusalem during the days of Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.9","r":"Neh.11.9","rawR":"Neh.11.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.9","value":"Neh.11.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. One of the leaders of the Levites who returned with Zerubbabel and Jeshua to Judah after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.8","r":"Neh.12.8","rawR":"Neh.12.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.8","value":"Neh.12.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. One of the princes of Judah who participated in the dedication of the Jerusalem wall during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.34","r":"Neh.12.34","rawR":"Neh.12.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.34","value":"Neh.12.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. One of the priests who played a musical instrument at the dedication of the Jerusalem wall during the days of Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.36","r":"Neh.12.36","rawR":"Neh.12.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.36","value":"Neh.12.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:36"},"). He is perhaps identical with #5 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Joseph’s son, father of Simeon and an ancestor of Jesus Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.30","r":"Luke.3.30","rawR":"Luke.3.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.30","value":"Luke.3.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:30"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JudahPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 35:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.23","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.23","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.1"},{"anchorText":"Gn 29:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.29.35","rawQueryValue":"Gen.29.35","sourceRefExact":"Gen.29.35"},{"anchorText":"Gn 38:3-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.3-5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.3-5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.3-5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.3","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.3","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.3"},{"anchorText":"Gn 38:29-30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.29-30","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.29-30","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.29-30"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.4"},{"anchorText":"Ex 1:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.1.2","rawQueryValue":"Exod.1.2","sourceRefExact":"Exod.1.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 46:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.12","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.12","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.12"},{"anchorText":"Nm 1:26-27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.1.26-27","rawQueryValue":"Num.1.26-27","sourceRefExact":"Num.1.26-27"},{"anchorText":"Gn 38:6-30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.6-30","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.6-30","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.6-30"},{"anchorText":"44:14-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.44.14-18","rawQueryValue":"Gen.44.14-18","sourceRefExact":"Gen.44.14-18"},{"anchorText":"49:8-12","canoni